questions.explanation:
$$A = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 2  \cr 
   { - 1} &amp; 4  \cr 

 } } \right],|A| = 6$$

${A^{ - 1}} = {{adjA} \over {|A|}} = {1 \over 6}\left[ {\matrix{
   4 &amp; { - 2}  \cr 
   1 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   {{2 \over 3}} &amp; { - {1 \over 3}}  \cr 
   {{1 \over 6}} &amp; {{1 \over 6}}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$

$$\left[ {\matrix{
   {{2 \over 3}} &amp; { - {1 \over 3}}  \cr 
   {{1 \over 6}} &amp; {{1 \over 6}}  \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   \alpha  &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; \alpha   \cr 

 } } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
   \beta  &amp; {2\beta }  \cr 
   { - \beta } &amp; {4\beta }  \cr 

 } } \right]$$

$$\left. \matrix{
  \alpha  + \beta  = {2 \over 3} \hfill \cr 
  \beta  =  - {1 \over 6} \hfill \cr}  \right\} \Rightarrow \alpha  = {2 \over 3} + {1 \over 6} = {5 \over 6}$$

$$ \therefore $$ $$4(\alpha  - \beta ) = 4(1) = 4$$

